  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "warning",
      "message": "Version 02 not confirmed to match 00/01. igus's drawing (p. 6) is of 'ReBeL-6DOF-00', and the ROS model's version 01 includes version 00's description. No public page describing 6DOF-02 was found (docs/research/2026-11-06-lab-machines.md, second update). The lab's arm has a connector box on its foot's back, which igus's drawing does not show; 02 may be the version with control in the base [INFERENCE]."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "message": "[INFERENCE, by arithmetic] The URDF's limits agree with igus's once its origin offsets are added: joints 2 and 3 are limited to +-110 degrees about origins turned +30 degrees, which gives -80 to +140 degrees from the straight-up zero; joint 5 to -87.5 to +102.5 degrees about an origin turned -7.5 degrees, which gives +-95 degrees. That the offsets are measured from igus's zero is the inference."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "message": "The URDF's link offsets (0.249, 0.2384, 0.289 and 0.122 m, foot to joint 2, joint 2 to 3, joint 3 to 5, joint 5 to the flange) differ from igus's X1 to X4 (252, 237, 297, 126 mm) by 1 to 8 mm, and two carry the comment 'TODO The 0.03m offset are most likely caused by the mesh file (Issue 15)'. The twin's sizes are checked against igus's drawing; its joint axes follow the URDF."
    },
    {
      "severity": "warning",
      "ref": "joint1",
      "message": "Not confirmed: where joint 1's zero points on the base. The twin takes it as the arm's front, the side away from the connector box (Daniel, 2026-11-09) [INFERENCE]. The lab's control software shows the real angles (the plan's visit list)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "message": "Which hand model matches the lab's hand is not confirmed: LinkerBot's and Realhand's L20 models differ in joint names and limits (docs/lab-machines-plan.md). The hand is one labelled part on the flange until Phase 7 (Daniel, 2026-11-09)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "message": "The name on Dr. Li's website lists a SCHUNK EGP gripper and a CobotPump; neither is on the arm in the photos of 2026-11-05, where the hand alone is on the flange."
    }
  ]
